## Requirements

- Python >= {{ python_version }}
- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)

## Getting started

```bash
git init                     # if the project is not a git repository yet
uv sync                      # create .venv and install the project + dev tools
uv run pre-commit install    # enable git hooks
```

**Commit the generated `uv.lock` file.** CI runs with `--locked`, so it fails if the lockfile is missing or out of sync with `pyproject.toml` (the `uv-lock` pre-commit hook keeps it updated locally).

## Development

| Task                      | Command                                   |
| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Run tests (with coverage) | `uv run pytest`                           |
| HTML coverage report      | `uv run pytest --cov-report=html`         |
| Lint                      | `uv run ruff check .`                     |
| Lint and autofix          | `uv run ruff check --fix .`               |
| Format                    | `uv run ruff format .`                    |
| Type check (strict)       | `uv run mypy`                             |
| Run all pre-commit hooks  | `uv run pre-commit run --all-files`       |
| Update hook versions      | `uv run pre-commit autoupdate`            |
| Add a dependency          | `uv add <package>`                        |
| Add a dev dependency      | `uv add --dev <package>`                  |

Tests fail if coverage drops below **{{ coverage_threshold }}%** (`[tool.coverage.report] fail_under` in `pyproject.toml`).

